    "turn_text": "You know, on virtually every major topic of the COVID pandemic, he's been on both sides of the issue in private. He's often been honest in public. He's almost always lied. You know, ask early on by a coworker whether or not the mask work he honestly responded in private that the pores in the mass were too large and it really wasn't worthwhile and that studies that indicated it wasn't worthwhile in public. He wears three masks. you know in in private he acknowledged and actually in the past as acknowledged that natural immunity uh... tends to work if you've had the flu you don't need a flu shot he said in two thousand four famously on c-spam but then he became uncertain with covid is that we don't know if natural immunity is going to work uh... on schools he was uh... for the lockdowns till he was against them till he was for until he was against them so just depended on the audience he was for but what was remarkable about his testimony was that he uh... couldn't recall over a hundred times you know he was smart enough to tell us the what to do and to mandate all these things about our behavior but uh... a hundred times he couldn't recall uh... when asked questions about these things are how they came about You're right on the social distancing on standing six feet apart. I mean, these are ridiculous things. I remember going to my son's university and outside in the grassy quad of the university, they had circles and you're supposed to stand in the circle six feet away from someone outside and talk to them. The plexiglass. of these things were based on science, and yet every day we were berated by CNN in the left. Oh, obey the science. The right doesn't want to obey the science. The science was all concocted in basically just opinions of people on the left, so they could do something. They wanted to do something. But in reality, none of the things they made us do had any effect on the virus.",
